{
  "_ulid": "01KK4F027ZMTQBCW246BY56Y37",
  "slugs": [],
  "title": "Fix task list automation filter showing wrong subset",
  "type": "task",
  "description": "The automation filter dropdown on the task list page shows All/Eligible/Blocked options but the filter does not work correctly — selecting 'Eligible' shows all pending tasks instead of only automation-eligible ones. The dropdown options should be: All, Eligible, Needs Review, Manual Only (not 'Blocked' which is a task status, not an automation status).",
  "spec_ref": "@web-dashboard",
  "meta_ref": null,
  "plan_ref": null,
  "status": "pending_review",
  "blocked_by": [],
  "depends_on": [],
  "context": [],
  "priority": 2,
  "tags": [
    "bug",
    "web-ui"
  ],
  "vcs_refs": [],
  "session_id": "01KK4FNHREW2HSWYXYW0ZNCJH6",
  "created_at": "2026-03-07T15:35:00.095Z",
  "started_at": "2026-03-07T15:46:59.097Z",
  "submitted_at": "2026-03-07T15:55:21.721Z",
  "notes": [
    {
      "_ulid": "01KK4FV0TPNJW69DE7B9K1VTS8",
      "created_at": "2026-03-07T15:49:43.382Z",
      "author": "@claude",
      "content": "Execution context:\n- Bug: Automation filter dropdown had wrong options (All/Eligible/Blocked) and daemon API ignored the automation query param\n- Root cause 1: TaskFilters.svelte used 'blocked' as an automation value but valid values are eligible/needs_review/manual_only\n- Root cause 2: Daemon GET /api/tasks route didn't include automation in query schema or filtering logic (static API was correct)\n- Fix: Updated dropdown to All/Eligible/Needs Review/Manual Only, added automation filtering to daemon route, fixed duplicate automation property in response\n- Files: packages/web-ui/src/lib/components/TaskFilters.svelte, packages/daemon/src/routes/tasks.ts",
      "supersedes": null,
      "superseded": false
    }
  ],
  "todos": [],
  "automation": "eligible",
  "_sourceFile": "/home/chapel/Projects/kynetic-spec-ui/.kspec/project.tasks.yaml",
  "inherited_traits": [
    {
      "ref": "@trait-filterable-list",
      "title": "Filterable List Commands",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-1",
          "given": "list command supports filtering",
          "when": "--status <value> provided",
          "then": "only items with matching status shown"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-2",
          "given": "list command supports filtering",
          "when": "--tag <value> provided",
          "then": "only items with matching tag shown"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-3",
          "given": "list command supports pagination",
          "when": "--limit N provided",
          "then": "output shows at most N items"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-4",
          "given": "list command supports pagination",
          "when": "--offset N provided",
          "then": "output skips first N items"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-5",
          "given": "multiple filters provided",
          "when": "--status X --tag Y used together",
          "then": "output shows items matching all filters (AND logic)"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-6",
          "given": "no items match filters",
          "when": "list command executes",
          "then": "empty list shown with informative message"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-7",
          "given": "list command output",
          "when": "results are displayed",
          "then": "summary shows total matching items and filter state"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-8",
          "given": "list command supports count mode",
          "when": "--count flag is provided",
          "then": "outputs only the total number of matching items as a plain integer (no item details); ignores --limit and --offset; in JSON mode outputs {\"count\": N}"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "ref": "@trait-websocket-protocol",
      "title": "WebSocket Protocol Patterns",
      "acceptance_criteria": [
        {
          "id": "ac-1",
          "given": "WebSocket connection is established",
          "when": "client connects",
          "then": "server assigns unique connection ID and sends connected event with session_id"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-2",
          "given": "client wants notifications",
          "when": "subscribe command sent with topics array",
          "then": "server tracks subscription and sends ack with request_id"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-3",
          "given": "client is subscribed to topic",
          "when": "relevant change occurs",
          "then": "server broadcasts event with format {msg_id, seq, timestamp, topic, event, data}"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-4",
          "given": "WebSocket connection is active",
          "when": "30 seconds pass without activity",
          "then": "server sends ping frame"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-5",
          "given": "ping was sent",
          "when": "no pong received within 90 seconds",
          "then": "connection is closed with code 1001"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-6",
          "given": "server sends events",
          "when": "client cannot keep up (backpressure)",
          "then": "server pauses non-critical broadcasts until drain event"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-7",
          "given": "connection is closing",
          "when": "close initiated",
          "then": "use code 1000 for clean close, 1001 for timeout, 1011 for error"
        },
        {
          "id": "ac-8",
          "given": "client reconnects after disconnect",
          "when": "new connection established",
          "then": "client resets sequence tracking (lastSeqProcessed = -1) since server generates new sequence"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

